    "['map vlan [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set bridge-domains md3 vlan-id 2', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset bridge-domains md3 vlan-id 2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `map vlan 2` command associates a Connectivity Fault Management (CFM) Maintenance Association (MA) with VLAN 2. In Juniper, this is typically done by configuring the VLAN ID under a bridge domain that corresponds to the CFM maintenance domain (md3 in this case).\\n\\nThe Juniper equivalent creates a bridge domain named \"md3\" (matching the CFM domain) and assigns VLAN ID 2 to it, which serves the same purpose of associating the CFM configuration with the specific VLAN.', 'trans_template': 'set bridge-domains md3 vlan-id 2'}]]": 1,
