    "['remote-mep mep-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 remote-mep 4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 remote-mep 4\\n##\\n\\nThe Juniper equivalent of `remote-mep mep-id 4` configures a remote MEP (Maintenance End Point) with ID 4 under the specified maintenance domain (md3) and maintenance association (ma3) in Ethernet CFM (Connectivity Fault Management).', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 remote-mep 4'}]]": 1,
    "['remote-mep ccm-receive mep-id [parameter1] enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 remote-mep 4 continuity-check reception enable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here is the translated Juniper equivalent command for `remote-mep ccm-receive mep-id 4 enable`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 remote-mep 4 continuity-check reception enable\\n##\\n\\nThis command enables the reception of Continuity Check Messages (CCM) for the remote MEP with ID 4 in Juniper's CFM configuration, which is functionally equivalent to the Huawei command.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 remote-mep 4 continuity-check reception enable'}]]": 1,
    "['test-id [parameter1] mep [parameter2] remote-mep [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check transmission interval 1s', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check transmission interval 1s\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3 remote-mep 4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The `test-id 1 mep 3 remote-mep 4` command in Huawei configures a connectivity fault management test between MEP 3 and remote MEP 4.\\n2. In Juniper, this translates to setting up the remote MEP association under the CFM configuration.\\n3. Note that Juniper handles the test ID implicitly through the MEP/remote-MEP association.\\n4. The interval is configured separately in Juniper (shown in the first command for completeness).\\n5. The actual test initiation would typically be done via operational commands in Juniper rather than configuration.\\n\\nThe translation maintains the same logical relationship between MEP 3 and remote MEP 4 as in the Huawei configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check transmission interval 1s'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3 remote-mep 4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] storm-control [parameter4]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check transmission interval 1s\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3 remote-mep 4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The `test-id 1 mep 3 remote-mep 4` command in Huawei configures a connectivity fault management test between MEP 3 and remote MEP 4.\\n2. In Juniper, this translates to setting up the remote MEP association under the CFM configuration.\\n3. Note that Juniper handles the test ID implicitly through the MEP/remote-MEP association.\\n4. The interval is configured separately in Juniper (shown in the first command for completeness).\\n5. The actual test initiation would typically be done via operational commands in Juniper rather than configuration.\\n\\nThe translation maintains the same logical relationship between MEP 3 and remote MEP 4 as in the Huawei configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3 remote-mep 4'}]]": 1,
    "['loss-measure single-ended-synthetic continual send test-id [parameter1] interval [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check interval 1s', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family inet service input [parameter3]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the given Huawei CFM loss measurement configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check interval 1s\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 synthetic-loss-measurement single-ended test-id 1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command sets the CCM interval to 1000ms (1 second) which is required for synthetic loss measurement\\n2. The second command configures single-ended synthetic loss measurement for the specified test ID\\n3. Juniper implements this as two separate commands rather than one combined command like Huawei\\n4. The continual measurement is implied in Juniper's implementation by default when synthetic loss measurement is enabled\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check interval 1s'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 synthetic-loss-measurement single-ended test-id 1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family inet service input [parameter3]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the given Huawei CFM loss measurement configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 continuity-check interval 1s\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 synthetic-loss-measurement single-ended test-id 1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command sets the CCM interval to 1000ms (1 second) which is required for synthetic loss measurement\\n2. The second command configures single-ended synthetic loss measurement for the specified test ID\\n3. Juniper implements this as two separate commands rather than one combined command like Huawei\\n4. The continual measurement is implied in Juniper's implementation by default when synthetic loss measurement is enabled\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 synthetic-loss-measurement single-ended test-id 1'}]]": 1,
